    <h2>Top Hook Formulas for 2026</h2>
    <p>To make it easier for you, here are practical examples of the most powerful hooks working right now that you can instantly apply to your content:</p>

    <h3>1. The "Imminent Loss" Hook (FOMO)</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>The Principle:</strong> People fear losing what they have much more than they desire gaining something new.<br>
      <strong>Example:</strong> <em>"You're making this huge mistake every day in [Your Niche] without realizing it... look at the disaster it's causing!"</em>
    </p>

    <h3>2. The "Storytelling" Hook</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>The Principle:</strong> Humans are wired to love stories that involve challenges, conflict, and eventual success.<br>
      <strong>Example:</strong> <em>"A client came to me completely hopeless, saying it's impossible to reach this result... Look at what we achieved today!"</em>
    </p>

    <h3>3. The "Shock & Debunking" Hook</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>The Principle:</strong> Attacking a common misconception makes you look like an authority figure holding the ultimate truth.<br>
      <strong>Example:</strong> <em>"[Your Niche] companies are fooling you and want you to buy this product... Here is the shocking truth!"</em>
    </p>

    <h2>Daoline's Pro Tip: How to Deliver the Hook?</h2>
    <p>A brilliantly written hook isn't enough if your on-camera performance is weak. When shooting your content, strictly follow these rules:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>No Intros:</strong> Never start with a greeting. Jump directly into the hook to create a <em>Pattern Interrupt</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Body Language:</strong> Take a slight step toward the camera while delivering the hook to create dynamic visual movement.</li>
        <li><strong>On-Screen Text:</strong> The hook must be written in a large, clear font during the first 3 seconds to catch the attention of viewers watching on mute.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="note-box" style="background: rgba(37,99,235,0.08); border-color: rgba(37,99,235,0.3); border-left-color: #3b82f6;">
      <div class="note-box-title" style="color: #60a5fa;">The Viral Video Formula ✨</div>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 12px;">A hook alone is not enough. For a video to truly convert, follow this structure:</p>
      <ul style="margin-bottom: 0;">
          <li><b>0-3 Seconds:</b> The Hook (Grab attention immediately).</li>
          <li><b>3-10 Seconds:</b> Retention (Assure them they are in the right place and convince them to stay).</li>
          <li><b>10-45 Seconds:</b> True Value (Deliver the information or quick fix they came for).</li>
          <li><b>45-60 Seconds:</b> Direct CTA (Tell them exactly what to do next: Save, Follow, or Comment).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p>In conclusion, remember that attention is the most expensive currency in 2026. When you offer real value wrapped in a smart, scroll-stopping hook, you'll find the algorithm actively looking for you—not the other way around.</p>
